  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Two lighter nuclei combine to form a comparatively heavier nucleus by the relation given below:</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>X</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>+</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>X</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mmultiscripts><mo>=</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>Y</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></mmultiscripts></math></p><p>&nbsp;The binding energies per nucleon <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>X</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mmultiscripts></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mmultiscripts><mi>Y</mi><mprescripts></mprescripts><mn>2</mn><mn>4</mn></mmultiscripts></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mi>MeV</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>MeV</mi></math> respectively. The energy released in this process is_____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>MeV</mi></math>.</p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "26",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Energy released in the given process <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo></math> Binding energy of product <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo></math> Binding energy of reactants.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>26</mn><mi>MeV</mi></math></p></blockquote>"
